why={
'S01':'End-to-end one-store boundary is present, but the company/organization clientele and example equipment types from T006 are absent.','S05':'The receive-versus-re-lendable distinction is recovered; the motivating next-morning search/alternative and cross-role shared view are not explicitly recorded.','S06':'No Low/Medium/High rating was spoken; silence is appropriate.','U01':'Responsibility and estimate-to-decision handoff are held open; the undecided repair charge stays out.','U02':'Proxy verification is marked pending the manager, without invented eligibility rule.','U03':'The two possible email times are retained as unresolved; no holiday-email fee result is asserted.','U04':'The fee table and amounts are pending; the change-related cancellation detail is not separately named.','U05':'Follow-up timing remains unresolved and no-reply confirmation is refused.','U06':'The operational comparison is stated without an invented precise arithmetic formula.','U07':'The transcript requires billing destination and identifying number but never assigns their storage to the reservation sheet; lines cited assert that location. No channel for accounting handoff is invented.','P01':'The barcode suggestion is not adopted as an operating rule; omission of the rejected proposal is acceptable.','O01':'Customer exchanges are covered, but company/organization identity from T006 is not.','O02':'Known reservation-sheet fields are recovered; reservation number and billing destination are asserted as sheet fields although their storage location is unsaid in T008 and T068.','A1-I4':'Oracle overstates the medium for a preparation-failure handoff: T040 says warehouse returns the failure to reception, not that it is written on a ticket. Shortage/fault ticket data are recovered. Draft line 350 cites an unreturned situation on the ticket; an empty return-time entry might support that reading, but actual ticket use in overdue checking is unconfirmed.','A1-P5':'Corrected prior-business-day 17:00 free-cancellation cutoff is in the initial pending-note, so it is recovered semantically; the cancellation procedure fails to cross-reference it. Sunday closure is only in preparation.','A1-P6':'The fee-bearing cancellation handoff is grounded, but line 264 additionally sends every cancellation to calculation staff, exceeding T024/T066.','A1-WHEN':'Oracle overstates communication channels: T016/T024 support phone and email for new/cancellation, T049 supports a phone extension, and change channel is unspecified. Draft preserves the grounded timing and does not invent the change channel.','A1-O3':'Main customer responses and consultations are grounded; lines 224 and 270 add outward change/cancellation result notices that T024/T046/T048 do not specify.','A2-P2':'Customer reconciliation, accessory check and signature are covered, but T026 explicitly says payment is afterward and the draft does not state this at the handoff.','A3-WHEN':'Warehouse checks when free, but the explicit no-same-day guarantee and possible next-morning inspection from T014 are missing.','A4-I5':'Billing destination was collected at reception, but its placement in the reservation sheet at line 628 has no transcript basis.','HIDDEN01':'Not spoken and no transcript cue; no recovery or question obligation, no positive credit.','HIDDEN02':'Not spoken and no transcript cue; no recovery or question obligation, no positive credit.','HIDDEN03':'Not spoken and no transcript cue; no recovery or question obligation, no positive credit.'}
